To best describe the atmosphere, menu, decor and service, I would only use the same name that is so synonymous with greatness; Old Fashion. I have decided to finally visit this, beautiful establishment with my girl for some drinks after sushi night. Right of the bat, as we dragged our tired bodies in,we were greeted by not one but three beautiful servers that offered menus and sitting immediately. After taking our sit at the bar, a bartender named Anna took it upon herself to personally make sure our first visit will be worth our while. I ordered the "Old Fashioned"  ($9) and my girl went for the Kitty ($10). We took our drinks and moved to the two couches placed at the entrance for a more comfortable conversation setting. The happy hour menu is simple and tasty (the way it should be!!!), offering both healthy and naughty dishes to choose from; interesting variety that includes Brussels Sprouts, Parmesan Fries and even Steak Bites. 
If your goal is to go out in order to see and be seen, I wouldn't recommend this tasteful, cozy place for you... It's not as superficial and shallow as you are...(;
But, if you are looking for a great selection of Rye and Classic bourbons accompanied by great service, than go check it out ASAP.

Commander's Palace was a complete disappointment.   For a place known for their service it was one disaster after another.   Here is the list of errors:
- cocktail waitress was not familiar with what is written in the menu;
- extra long wait to get the dinner menus;
- it took 45 minutes and 6 requests to get cream for coffee;
- bar ran out of cucumbers for Pimms cocktails;
- staff forgot to serve us bread; 
- staff left appetizer plate on table throughout dinner and dessert; 
- cleared dinner plates and never asked if we wanted leftovers;
- waiter never asked 2 members of our party of 6 if they wanted dessert; 
- had to repeatedly ask for water refills; 
- cocktail waitress did not know what beers were being served,  then writes down on a piece of paper.  After one of us orders a beer,  she returns to say that they no longer serve that beer;
- waiter and the menu do not disclose the up charge for cheesecake as a dessert.

If not for most of the food being really good, this ranking would have been 1 star.
